    <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
        <link:loc xlink:href="#f-110" xlink:label="f-110_lbl" xlink:type="locator" />
        <link:loc xlink:href="#f-400" xlink:label="f-400_lbl" xlink:type="locator" />
        <link:loc xlink:href="#f-1115" xlink:label="f-1115_lbl" xlink:type="locator" />
        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-110_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-110_47338_lbl" />
        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-400_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-400_47393_lbl" />
        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-1115_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-1115_47440_lbl" />
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-110_47338_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><div><p>The following are the intermediary companies in the chain of ownership between Energy Transfer LP (DE) and ET CC Holdings LLC (DE):</p><p>Energy Transfer LP (DE) owns 100% in ET CC Holdings LLC (DE). ET CC Holdings LLC (DE) owns 83.8% of Inland Corporation (OH). </p></div><div class="Section0"><p class="_Normal_"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal"><br /></span></p><p style="text-align: left; page-break-inside: auto; page-break-after: auto; page-break-before: avoid; line-height: 107.916664%; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"><span style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; line-height: 107.916664%"><br /></span></p><p style="text-align: left; page-break-inside: auto; page-break-after: auto; page-break-before: avoid; line-height: 107.916664%; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"><span style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; line-height: 107.916664%"><br /></span></p></div></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-400_47393_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $1.8 million are included in Account(s) 600.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1115_47440_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">The cost of service results were calculated using the Cost of Service Model. This Model calculates cost of service using the Trended Original Cost methodology promulgated by the FERC in Opinion No. 154-B, 31 FERC 61,377 (1985), as modified and clarified by subsequent rulings.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>